Enhancement: lock parity Phase 3 durable prune plans

Prune now persists an encrypted additive `prune_plan` config extension after
replacement indexes are uploaded and before normal deletion. The marker records
the exact old index/pack candidates and replacement indexes. Deferred cleanup
(`prune --keep-delete`) is finalized by a later plain `prune` only after vaultic
revalidates that all replacement indexes exist and no surviving current index
references a candidate pack.

Deletion is restricted to IDs explicitly stored in the marker. Immediate prune
uses the same marker and rewrite-captured index IDs before cleanup. Durable plan
storage requires atomic config replacement; unsupported backends fail safely
instead of risking a missing config singleton. Restic and rustic ignore the
additive config extension.

